    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d480">

                <pb facs="0629" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/370</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-11-14">November 14, 1929</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1399</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department has received your despatch
                    No. 2372 of October 11, 1929,<anchor n="13" xml:id="d480-f1"/> in regard to the
                    occupation of American mission premises by Chinese troops.</p>
                <pb facs="0630" n="486" xml:id="pg486"/>
                <p>The Department approves the instruction issued to the American Consulate at
                    Tsinan by the Legation under date of October 9, 1929, a copy of which was
                    enclosed with the despatch under acknowledgment.</p>
                <p>The Department would be interested in receiving information regarding the results
                    that may follow a direct appeal by American missionaries to the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs in cases of occupation of mission property by Chinese
                    troops.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson
                            Trusler Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
